From: "Juan J. Sanchez" <jjsanchez@igalia.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 19:07:38 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] [WPE][Android] Let hidden pages that change their title go
 idle Need the bug URL (OOPS!).

Reviewed by NOBODY (OOPS!).

Before this change, on every platform but iPhone, a page that changed its title
without user action got a background activity, so that its process kept running
while the page was hidden. Where suspended processes keep running (WPE on
Android), the page went on updating its title without it, and the activity only
ranked its process above hidden pages and the processes of other apps, which
Android then ended first when memory ran low.

This change no longer takes the activity where suspended processes keep
running, as it is not taken on iPhone either.

No new tests (OOPS!).

* Source/WebKit/UIProcess/WebPageProxy.cpp:
(WebKit::WebPageProxy::didReceiveTitleForFrame):
---
 Source/WebKit/UIProcess/WebPageProxy.cpp | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/WebPageProxy.cpp b/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/WebPageProxy.cpp
index b37209b950..7e2490b26d 100644
--- a/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/WebPageProxy.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/WebPageProxy.cpp
@@ -11751,7 +11751,13 @@ void WebPageProxy::didReceiveTitleForFrame(IPC::Connection& connection, FrameIde
 #if PLATFORM(IOS_FAMILY)
         deviceClassIsSmallScreen = PAL::deviceClassIsSmallScreen();
 #endif
-        if (!deviceClassIsSmallScreen) {
+        // Where suspended processes keep running, a hidden page goes on updating its title anyway, and the activity
+        // would only make the system end other processes first.
+        bool suspendedProcessesKeepRunning = false;
+#if HAVE(RUNNING_SUSPENDED_PROCESSES)
+        suspendedProcessesKeepRunning = true;
+#endif
+        if (!deviceClassIsSmallScreen && !suspendedProcessesKeepRunning) {
             bool isTitleChangeLikelyDueToUserAction = false;
 
 #if !PLATFORM(IOS_FAMILY)
